@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Confirmed deletion without false success or media loss
hide footbox
autonumber
actor Maintainer
participant "app : App" as App
participant "messagebox\n<<external>>" as Dialog
participant "dataset\n<<module>>" as Dataset
activate Maintainer
Maintainer -> App : _delete_browse_entry()
activate App
alt No selected ID
  note over App : Explain selection requirement; do not write.
else Entry selected
  App -> Dialog : askyesno(Delete entry, prompt)
  activate Dialog
  Dialog --> App : Yes / No
  deactivate Dialog
  alt No / dismissed
    note over App : Preserve row, selection, draft and audio.
  else Yes
    App -> Dataset : delete_entry(selected_id)
    activate Dataset
    note over Dataset : Locked read; require a matching ID.\nRemove matching IDs and atomically replace CSV.
    Dataset --> App : Commit / EntryNotFoundError / storage failure
    deactivate Dataset
    alt Missing ID or storage failure
      note over App : Explain failure; preserve unsaved editor fields.\nNo Entry deleted success message.
    else Commit succeeded
      App -> App : _clear_browse_selection()
      activate App
      App --> App : Cleared selected ID, fields and audio reference
      deactivate App
      App -> Dataset : load_all() through _refresh_views()
      activate Dataset
      Dataset --> App : Shared snapshot or reported refresh error
      deactivate Dataset
      note over App : Report committed deletion.\nThe linked saved audio file is retained.
    end
  end
end
App --> Maintainer : Current truthful status
deactivate App
deactivate Maintainer
legend bottom
  Preserved desktop compatibility only; the authenticated web workspace has separate revisions.
  Confirmation is a decision, not an authorization or authentication check.
  Atomic replacement protects write integrity; there is no undo stack.
endlegend
@enduml
